## Chemical etching of ZIF-8 by tannic acid ● Timing 6 h
13 Add $1.25\mathrm{g}$ of tannic acid and then $50~\mathrm{mL}$ of DIW into a $50\mathrm{-mL}$ glass vial. Close the vial with its cap and sonicate the mixture. Tannic acid dissolves in DIW upon sonication for $60~\mathrm{{min}}$ yielding a clear brownish tannic acid solution.
14 Transfer $5~\mathrm{mL}$ of the ZIF-8 dispersion $(0.100\ \mathrm{g/mL})$ and then $45~\mathrm{mL}$ of DIW to a $150\mathrm{-mL}$ beaker containing a magnetic stirring bar ${(40-}\mathrm{{mm}}$ length and $8\mathrm{-mm}$ diameter).
