3 Pour the zinc precursor solution into the organic linker solution at a steady rate. CRITICAL STEP Remove any air bubbles formed at the center of the mixture by using a disposable pipette to minimize any possible disruption of nucleation and growth of ZIF-8 seed.   
4 Stir the mixture of the zinc precursor solution and the organic linker solution at $200~\mathrm{rpm}$ for $10~\mathrm{min}$ .   
5 After $10\ \mathrm{min}$ , stop the stirring, remove the magnetic stirring bar ( $_{40-\mathrm{{mm}}}$ length and $8\mathrm{-mm}$ diameter), transfer the mixture into the $100\mathrm{-mL}$ Teflon vessel with a lid and place in an autoclave.   
6 Close the autoclave tightly and place it in an air-forced oven at $100~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $^{12\mathrm{~h~}}$ (Fig. 4a). PAUSE POINT ZIF-8 seed with a diameter of $50~\mathrm{~nm}$ will be synthesized by adding polyvinylpyrrolidone (PVP) into the mixture of the zinc precursor solution and the organic linker solution and then aging the mixture at room temperature (Table 1 and Extended Data Fig. 2a). ZIF8 seed with a diameter of $500~\mathrm{nm}$ is synthesized when the mixture of zinc precursor solution and organic linker solution is aged at room temperature in the absence of PVP (Table 1 and Extended Data Fig. 2d).   
7 After $^{12\mathrm{~h},}$ allow the autoclave to cool to room temperature and then carefully transfer the white dispersion into $50\mathrm{-mL}$ centrifuge tubes.   
8 Centrifuge the collected ZIF-8 seed dispersion at 3,273 r.c.f. for $15~\mathrm{min}$ . A supernatant solution is discarded, and then the white pellet is resuspended in $40~\mathrm{mL}$ of methanol. CRITICAL STEP To resuspend the pellet more easily, first add $10~\mathrm{mL}$ of methanol and shake the tube vigorously to break the pellet and then add the remaining $30~\mathrm{mL}$ of methanol. With the cap closed, repeatedly and briefly sonicate $(\sim30\ s)$ and vigorously shake the solution to further break the pellet. ? TROUBLESHOOTING
